  "acquisition": {
    "strategy": "url_list",
    "description": "One SPARQL request per (property, page). The inner subquery orders by (item, value) and takes LIMIT/OFFSET over that total order, so the pages of a property are a complete, disjoint partition and each page is independently re-runnable. Each property is followed by at least one empty page, which is what lets the pipeline tell \"the property ended here\" from \"this response was truncated\". The total order is also this route's size limit: measured on 2026-09-19, the query service answers the sorted inner subquery for every declared property but times out (HTTP 500/502/504) on P496, whose 2,065,452 statements it cannot sort inside its 60-second limit at any page size, including LIMIT 100. See docs/wikidata-bridge.md. desired_bytes is measured, not estimated: the 2026-09-19 acquisition of these 31 properties transferred 43,169,561 bytes and wrote 43,361,124 to disk, and 65,000,000 is that on-disk figure plus 50% headroom for Wikidata's growth between acquisitions. The previous 250,000,000 was a pre-acquisition estimate carrying headroom for P496 (ORCID), which this declaration does not acquire.",
    "documentation": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:SPARQL_query_service/queries",
    "desired_bytes": 65000000,
    "priority": 1.0,
    "url_template": "https://query.wikidata.org/sparql?query=SELECT%20%3Fitem%20%3Flabel%20%3Fvalue%20%28GROUP_CONCAT%28DISTINCT%20%3Ft%3BSEPARATOR%3D%22%7C%22%29%20AS%20%3Ftypes%29%20WHERE%20%7B%0A%20%20%7B%20SELECT%20%3Fitem%20%3Fvalue%20WHERE%20%7B%20%3Fitem%20wdt%3A{property}%20%3Fvalue%20.%20{filter}%20%7D%0A%20%20%20%20ORDER%20BY%20%3Fitem%20%3Fvalue%20LIMIT%20{limit}%20OFFSET%20{offset}%20%7D%0A%20%20OPTIONAL%20%7B%20%3Fitem%20wdt%3AP31%20%3Fc%20.%20BIND%28STRAFTER%28STR%28%3Fc%29%2C%22%2Fentity%2F%22%29%20AS%20%3Ft%29%20%7D%0A%20%20SERVICE%20wikibase%3Alabel%20%7B%20bd%3AserviceParam%20wikibase%3Alanguage%20%22en%2Cmul%22.%20%3Fitem%20rdfs%3Alabel%20%3Flabel.%20%7D%0A%7D%20GROUP%20BY%20%3Fitem%20%3Flabel%20%3Fvalue",
